('alict_02606', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following attributes is NOT typically used with the <img> tag in', '["src", "alt", "title", "href", "class"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The attribute that is NOT typically used with the specifically for embedding images in a and the common attributes used with it • src Specifies the URL of the image', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2606, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02607', 8, 'Web Development', 'What happens to the content inside a CSS comment during rendering?', '["It is rendered as hidden text", "It is displayed in the console logs", "It is shown as plain text in the browser", "It is ignored by the browser", "It causes an error"]'::jsonb, 4, 'CSS comments ( intended for developers to leave notes or explanations within the and they do not affect the visual rendering or functionality of the web page. CSS ( The correct answer is 4) It is ignored by the browser', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2607, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02608', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following CSS properties can be used to create a responsive layout by making an element adjust its width based on the parent element''s size?', '["width", "max-width", "min-width", "display", "flex"]'::jsonb, 5, 'The flex property is used to create flexible layouts. It allows elements to adjust their size based on the available space within their making it ideal for responsive designs', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2608, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02609', 8, 'Web Development', 'What is the purpose of the text-decoration property in CSS?', '["To change the font family of the text", "To add special effects like or strikethroughs to the text. ioyd strikethrough jeks", "To adjust the line height and spacing between characters", "To apply colors to text", "To apply borders and background colors to text"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This option is false. The text-decoration property does not change the font family of the text. Changing the font family of the text is done using the font-family property in not the text- decoration property. Option 2: This option is true', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2609, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02610', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following properties is NOT part of the CSS box model?', '["Font-size", "Margin", "Padding", "Border", "Width"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct font-size The font-size property is related to text styling and is not part of the box which deals with layout and spacing. font-size', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2610, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02611', 8, 'Web Development', 'Consider the following CSS', '["Blue", "Red", "No color will be applied", "Transparent", "Undefined"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The given CSS contains two h1 but the second one is commented out using comments are ignored by the meaning the second h1 rule CSS h1 folla wvx', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2611, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02612', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following cannot be used as a measuring unit in CSS?', '["rem", "ch", "px", "cm", "vx"]'::jsonb, 5, 'The correct answer is 5) as it is not a valid measuring unit in CSS. CSS supports various measurement units for defining including relative units (e.g., and absolute units (e.g., vx is not recognized as a valid unit in CSS specifications', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2612, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02613', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following is true about the <meta> tag in', '["It is used to create navigation links between different pages. th", "It must always be placed inside the", "It can be used to specify character viewport and metadata. th", "It is required for all documents to be valid", "It is used to define styles and scripts within an document. th"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The section. It does not display content directly on the page but helps define settings and other information for the browser or search engines. th Common uses of the <meta> tag include • Character Encoding The ensuring proper display of especially for non-English characters', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2613, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02614', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following is NOT a valid CSS property?', '["color", "font-size", "text-decoration", "border-radius", "text-align-vertical"]'::jsonb, 5, 'This question asks us to identify which of the given options is not a valid CSS property. CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) is used in web development to style defining properties like and decoration of content on a webpage', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2614, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02615', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following statements about CSS specificity and rule application is true?', '["An element with a class selector always overrides an ID selector", "Inline styles have lower specificity than external CSS files", "If two selectors have the same the one defined last in the CSS file wins. jrl folla tlu", "Universal selector (*) has higher specificity than element selectors. Universal (*)", "External CSS always overrides inline styles regardless of specificity"]'::jsonb, 3, 'This is correct. When two rules apply to the same element and have equal the browser chooses the one that appears later in the CSS file. The idea is that newer rules should have the power to override earlier ones if they target the same thing with the same weight', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2615, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02616', 8, 'Web Development', '<a href = "sabaragamuwa.html" target', '["Same window", "Same frame", "A window called \"-blank \"", "A frame called \"-blank \"", "New window"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "New window". This follows from standard HTML/CSS behaviour for the tag or property in question.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2616, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02617', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following CSS selectors correctly applies bold text styling to an element with the ID "ID1" and a class "Class1"?', '["@ID1, .Class1 {", "#ID1, .Class1 {", "ID1, Class1 {", "$ID1, #Class1 {", "$ID1, *Class1 {"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In to target an element by its you use the '' # '' symbol followed by the ID name (e.g., #ID1). To target an element by its you use a '' . '' followed by the class name (e.g., .Class1). If you want to apply the same styling rule to multiple you can separate them with a comma', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2617, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02618', 8, 'Web Development', 'Choose the best statement about the code given', '["The above code will give an error", "The above code will not change anything on the website", "It is a CSS code", "This code will make the CSS file longer to load", "This is a shorthand property in CSS shorthand"]'::jsonb, 5, 'This won''t give any the code will change the background colour and add a background image if the image is in the same folder as the it is a CSS code but there is a more suitable this code won''t make the CSS file longer to load rather it will make it faster', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2618, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02619', 8, 'Web Development', 'What is the correct CSS rule to set the background colour of a web page to green?', '["body { body-color : \"green\" }", "body { background-colour : green", "body { bgcolor :", "body { background-color : green", "body { bgcolor = \"green\" }"]'::jsonb, 4, 'This answer is incorrect because there is no CSS property called body-color. the value should be without quotation marks. body-color 2) This answer is incorrect because the property background-colour is misspelled. The correct property name is background-color', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2619, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02620', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following properties is NOT part of the CSS box model fldgila fkdjkafka : 1) Explanation of each option', '["font-size The font-size property is related to text styling and is not part of the box which deals with layout and spacing. font-size", "margin is part of the box model and defines the space outside the element''s border. margin", "padding is part of the box model and defines the space between the element''s content and its border. padding", "border is part of the box model and defines the boundary around the element''s padding and content. border", "width is part of the box model and defines the size of the content area. width"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "font-size The font-size property is related to text styling and is not part of the box which deals with layout and spacing. font-size". This follows from standard HTML/CSS behaviour for the tag or property in question.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2620, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02621', 8, 'Web Development', 'What happens if you apply this CSS to a div?', '["The entire border is red", "Only the top border is visible", "No border appears", "Border color changes on hover", "The border is dotted"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The 5px solid 5 pixels thick and solid in but completely transparent in color. This means that although the border exists and takes up space around the it is invisible to the eye because transparent means no color', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2621, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02622', 8, 'Web Development', 'What is not a use of anchor tag?', '["To link to another webpage", "To link to a section within the same page", "To create a form submission button", "To open an email client with a pre-filled email fmr ,o", "To download a file"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is a primary use of the Option 2: The same page. Option 3: The Option 4: The Option 5: The allow users to download a file', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2622, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
