('alict_02634', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following is the correct CSS syntax for selecting an element with the id "header"?', '["header {", "#header { }", "#header {", "*header {", "&header {"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: header {} → This targets fuys Option 2: #header { } which is invalid in CSS syntax. Option 3: #header { color. Option 4: *header {} Invalid. Universal selector * cannot be combined this way. Option 5: &header {}Not valid in plain jeks', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2634, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02635', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which CSS property is used to add space between the content and the border of an element?', '["margin", "border-spacing", "line-height", "letter-spacing", "padding"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: The margin property creates space outside the between the element and its neighboring elements. It does not affect the space inside the element. margin', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2635, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02636', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following is the primary purpose of indentation in CSS?', '["To make the CSS code run faster", "To improve the readability and maintainability of the code", "To reduce the file size of the CSS file", "To add extra spacing between CSS rules for the browser", "To change the specificity of CSS selectors"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Indentation in CSS is primarily used to improve readability and maintainability of the code. Well-indented CSS makes it easier for developers to understand the structure. CSS Indentation m%Odk', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2636, 'A/L Past Paper Series')
